  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-27T17:06:53.107Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The current Safety system seems to have an outside-in approach: players can choose what they don't want to see, using the shield levels.\n\nWhat if there was also an inside-out safety approach?: players could choose what they don't want other players to see, using a parallel shield level system.\n\nOutside-in safety: filter what one sees.\n\nInside-out safety: filter what one shares.\n\nIf a player doesn't want an aspect of their identity (e.g. bio, links, groups, worlds, avatar) to be visible to certain players, they could hide those aspects from certain user/trusted levels.\n\ne.g. only Friends and Trusted players could see a player's gender identity, so that player would (hopefully) be less likely to be bullied by transphobes, because that part of their identity is hidden.",
